<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event · other</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sáenz Peña Law</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1912</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sáenz Peña Law was the Argentine electoral law of 1912, promoted by President Roque Sáenz Peña, which established secret, universal and compulsory male suffrage for citizens and representation for minorities. It ended the electoral fraud of the conservative order and allowed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hipolito-yrigoyen">Hipólito Yrigoyen</a> of the Radical Civic Union to win the presidency in 1916.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/saenz-pena-law.jpg" alt="Sáenz Peña Law" width="320" height="327" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Carlos San Martín · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Museo_del_Bicentenario_-_Urna_electoral_de_1916.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
